// Game: Postretro
// Format: Standard
// Reflection blend-cost spike fixture. SPIKE BRANCH claude/blend-cost-spike.
// Axis-aligned box brushes; 1 map unit = 0.0254 m; map coordinates, Z up.
// Keep comments free of braces and quotes, and never leave a blank line
// inside an entity block. Fluid water is declared in content/dev/start-script.ts.
// ----
// Compile: cargo run --release -p postretro-level-compiler --bin prl-build -- content/dev/maps/reflection-blend-spike.map -o content/dev/maps/reflection-blend-spike.prl
// Brief:   context/plans/drafts/reflection-probe-seams--blend-cost-spike/index.md
// ----
// ROOM A, spike worst case: x 0 to 960, y 0 to 960, floor z 0, ceiling z 320,
//   about 24.4 by 24.4 by 8.1 m. ONE fluid_volume, pool x 96 to 864, y 96 to 864,
//   surface z 0, pit floor z -96, made of three abutting brushes split along x
//   at 352 and 608. Three authored reflection_volume boxes x 0 to 352, 352 to 608,
//   608 to 960, each y 0 to 960, z -96 to 320, abut and cover the room, so the
//   level has three probes on one plane. Four curve-animated lights, periods
//   900, 1300, 1700, 2300 ms, light every capture, so each probe stores K = 4.
//   Two static fills, three pillars in the water, rim crates, coloured walls.
// ROOM B, typical pose: canal hall B1 x 1024 to 1536 and B2 x 1552 to 2064,
//   y 0 to 512, ceiling z 320, wall x 1536 to 1552 with a doorway y 192 to 320,
//   z 0 to 128. ONE fluid_volume x 1088 to 2000, y 224 to 288, surface z -16, as
//   three brushes split at the doorway faces x 1536 and 1552: B1 run, doorway
//   piece, B2 run. No authored boxes; the derived probes bind B1, the doorway
//   piece and B2, three probes on one plane. One unsplit brush is one face
//   and so one derived probe for the whole canal, with no seam to blend.
//   Static lights only. A door x 960 to 1024, y 32 to 96 joins A and B1.
// ----
// CAPTURE POSES, engine coordinates: x = -map y, y = map z, z = -map x, metres.
//   Yaw 0 looks along map +x, yaw 90 along map +y. Capture pitch is limited to 89.
//   Worst case: room A centre, map 480 480 300, high, looking straight down:
//     position -12.192 7.62 -12.192, yaw_deg 0, pitch_deg -89, water fills the view.
//   Typical: room B1, map 1112 256 48, low eye over the canal looking east
//     along it through the doorway: position -6.5024 1.2192 -28.2448, yaw_deg 0, pitch_deg -6.
